# Nexus Exchange MCP server — environment variables.
# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit real secrets.

# Which network to target: testnet | mainnet | local | custom. Defaults to
# testnet (play funds — synthetic USDX, faucet-funded) when unset. An
# unrecognized value is an error, never a silent default: the spec's rule is that
# an unknown network is treated as real funds. `mainnet` has no reachable host yet
# and fails with an explanation — use NEXUS_EXCHANGE_API_URL to target it once its
# DNS is live (it then assumes the public-gateway shape, since this package ships
# no measured shape for a host it has never reached; describe a bare-indexer
# mainnet with the `custom` bundle and NEXUS_EXCHANGE_FUNDS=real instead).
# `custom` describes a stage of your own (see below). See the README "Networks"
# section.
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK=testnet

# Explicit ORIGIN override — scheme + host, not a surface path. Wins over
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK; leave unset to use the selected network's host. Must be
# http(s), with no embedded user:password@ and no query or fragment (it is
# concatenated with a request path). A value that still ends in /api/exchange is
# accepted and normalized, so it cannot double up.
#
# BOTH surfaces hang off this origin plus the gateway path below (ENG-6221): the
# public convention puts /api/v1 at /api/exchange/api/v1/..., while a bare
# indexer serves it at the origin. This URL only redirects the HOST; alongside a
# named network the network keeps its own shape, so NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK=local
# with a URL still serves both surfaces at that origin.
#
# SETTING THIS ALONE IS DEPRECATED. It names a host without saying whose money is
# behind it, so it resolves to a custom target with undeclared funds and the tools
# that cannot be undone refuse; the server prints one notice on stderr and then
# runs exactly as before — nothing is removed. With no network named there is no
# shape to read either, so the public-gateway convention is assumed and the notice
# says so. Set NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK=custom and the bundle below instead.
# Alongside a named network it is NOT deprecated: that target already declared
# its funds and the URL only redirects its host.
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_API_URL=

# ── A custom stage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The four variables below are read ONLY when NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK=custom, and
# setting one without it is an error rather than a silent no-op. Together with
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_API_URL they describe a deployment this package ships no
# hostname for. Uncomment all of NETWORK/LABEL/FUNDS to use it.
#
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK_LABEL is a name for the stage. Required, and restricted
# to letters, digits, ".", "_" and "-" (max 64) because the Nexus clients
# namespace stored credentials by it.
#
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_FUNDS says whose money is behind the URL: real | play | unknown.
# Required, with NO default — a staging deployment of mainnet holds real funds, so
# guessing either way is wrong. Until it is declared (or you select a named
# network), the tools that cannot be undone — place_order, amend_order, the
# deposit/margin tools, create_bridge_deposit_address — refuse to run.
#
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_FAUCET=1 declares that the stage HAS a faucet. Separate from
# funds and absent until declared: claim_faucet / claim_credit need play funds AND
# a faucet, so they refuse without this.
#
# NEXUS_EXCHANGE_GATEWAY_PATH is where the deployment hangs off the host:
# "/api/exchange" (default, the public gateway convention) or "/" for a bare
# indexer that serves at its root, like `local`. Since ENG-6221 it places BOTH
# surfaces — /api/v1 as well as the legacy routes — so getting it wrong 404s
# every tool, not only the legacy ones, and misdirects the minted WebSocket
# endpoint. Read only with NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK=custom, so reaching for it means
# filling in LABEL and FUNDS too.
#NEXUS_EXCHANGE_NETWORK_LABEL=
#NEXUS_EXCHANGE_FUNDS=
#NEXUS_EXCHANGE_FAUCET=
#NEXUS_EXCHANGE_GATEWAY_PATH=

# HMAC API credentials. Only required for account reads and trading
# (get_balance, get_positions, get_open_orders, place_order, cancel_order).
# Market-data tools work without these.
#
# For the stdio server these are the account it trades as. For the hosted
# Streamable HTTP server (npm run start:http) they are only a fallback — each
# HTTP session normally supplies its own credential via request headers
# (X-Nexus-Api-Key / X-Nexus-Api-Secret); see the README "Hosted HTTP server".
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_API_KEY=
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_API_SECRET=

# Session token (Bearer) from the `login` tool / POST /auth/login. Only needed
# for the API-key management tools (list_api_keys, create_api_key,
# delete_api_key), which authenticate with a session token rather than HMAC.
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Admin tier tools (list_tiers, set_tier, delete_tier) are operator-only and
# OFF by default. They use the gateway's admin secret and mutate other
# accounts' fee tiers — never enable on an untrusted agent surface. To opt in,
# set ENABLE_ADMIN_TOOLS=1 and provide the admin secret.
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_ENABLE_ADMIN_TOOLS=
NEXUS_EXCHANGE_ADMIN_SECRET=

# Hosted Streamable HTTP server (src/http-index.ts) listen config. Only used by
# `npm run start:http`. The MCP endpoint is served at MCP_HTTP_PATH and a
# liveness probe at /healthz.
MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_PATH=/mcp
